    "reviewed_conclusions": [
      "All 65 fixed-scope file hashes match disk; the scope contains all eight own formal pages and the actual item, UI/RAW, image, map/reverse, and source evidence.",
      "Both implementations correctly show cooldowns I-IV of 18/15/12/9 seconds and block-cost multipliers .85/.80/.75/.70, formatted as 15/20/25/30% lower cost; the passive stat remains installed without a held gate.",
      "A new deferred push requires an accepted on_block event with positive cost that actually depletes stamina, held source weapon when the proc event is handled, and an available cooldown. The first event is not delayed by an initial cooldown; successful handling starts its cooldown.",
      "The example assumes normalized incoming block cost 1.00, neutral other cost modifiers, and stamina .72. Tiers I-III exhaust stamina at .85/.80/.75; IV cost .70 does not. This correctly illustrates that reduced block cost can prevent a break; 1000 is PowerLevel input, not HP damage.",
      "The queued push flag is consumed on a later Buff update and uses then-current player position/facing. A slot switch stops new held-gated procs but does not remove the installed passive or cancel an already queued push. True unequip deletes this single nonpredicted Buff instance through the verified server removal path, so its pending push no longer runs.",
      "Ordinary incoming melee/ranged blocks remain subject to each action’s accepted type, angle, and stamina conditions. Slab-shield special block cost is zero and cannot break; Shock Maul Shield special windup/activation retains its documented .4-second incoming-block window. Outgoing push itself is not the incoming trigger.",
      "The RAW EN/ZH strings and four-tier formatter reconstruction match the fixed resource/hash. The tier table and variant pages separate both actual implementations and four model bindings; the verified icon path and attachment are kept distinct."
    ],
